                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Thinking about this a bit more, I think it's better if we have a json config that defines the dbus object, interface, property and the expected value for it to be valid for Available to be true. This will allow a lot more flexibility as I know for some of our IBM systems, we're going to have some specific openpower properties we want this to look at. I also think it will simplify some of the code trying to find these properties. We can have a default config provided in this repo that just looks at chassis presence."
                },
